### JWT Auth Guide — API test flow (VS Code REST Client)
### Or run the curl commands from the README.

@host = http://localhost:3000

### 0. Health check
GET {{host}}/api/health

### 1. Register (succeeds, sets cookies)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "sara", "email": "sara@example.com", "password": "passw0rd1" }

### 1b. Register validation failure (short password)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "sara", "email": "sara@example.com", "password": "short" }

### 1c. Register duplicate (409)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "sara", "email": "sara@example.com", "password": "passw0rd1" }

### 2. Protected route WITHOUT token (401)
GET {{host}}/api/users/me

### 3. Protected route WITH token (200)
GET {{host}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Login (set cookies; try 11x quickly to trigger the 429 rate limit)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "sara", "password": "passw0rd1" }

### 4b. Login with wrong password (401; does NOT count toward rate limit)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "sara", "password": "wrong-password" }

### 5. Refresh (rotates tokens; old refresh token is revoked)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh

### 6. Update profile (exercise #2)
PATCH {{host}}/api/users/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{ "email": "sara.new@example.com" }

### 7. Logout (revokes refresh token, clears cookies -> 204)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout

### 8. Refresh after logout (401 - revoked)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
